                <pb facs="0148" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C114/445d: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-23T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 23—1:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Department’s instruction 226, February 12. In a note dated August 21st the
                    Grand Duchy of Luxembourg accepts conditions and reserves contained in Senate
                    resolution for the adherence of the United States to the Permanent Court of
                    International Justice.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
